/* DATA DESCRIPTION:
Citation:	Xie, Yihao; Huang, Ting; Zhu, Aili; Lei, Jin; Fernández-Remolar, David C (2026): Element concentrations in phosphoritic limestone (102.6 m) from Los Lagares-1 drill core [dataset]. PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.993263
Abstract:	This dataset contains LA-ICP-MS trace element concentrations from phosphatized bioclasts and associated mineral phases in a phosphoritic limestone interval at 101.8 m depth in the Los Lagares-1 borehole (Pedroche Formation, Córdoba, Spain). The data include major, minor, and trace elements, including rare earth elements (REE), measured in carbonate fluorapatite (CFA) and surrounding matrix. The dataset provides information on elemental distributions and geochemical variability linked to phosphogenesis and early diagenetic processes. These data contribute to the reconstruction of paleoenvironmental conditions and nutrient dynamics in a Lower Cambrian reef–lagoon system.
Keyword(s):	Element geochemistry; Greenish siltstone; LA-ICP-MS; Lower Cambrian; major elements; Pedroche Formation; Phosphoritic limestone; REE; Spain; trace elements
Supplement to:	Xie, Yihao; Huang, Ting; Zhu, Aili; Lei, Jin; Fernández-Remolar, David C (in prep.): A multi-analytical approach to the study of phosphatic materials from the Lower Cambrian of Spain. Minerals
Documentation:	Target maps/photographs showing LA-ICP-MS spot locations for samples at 102.6 m (URI: https://download.pangaea.de/reference/138893/attachments/LA_targets_1026m.pdf)
Funding:	Ministry of Science and Technology of the People's Republic of China (MOST) (URI: http://en.most.gov.cn/eng/index.htm), grant/award no. 2021YFA0716100: Research on the habitable environments and biosignatures of Mars
